message: "Please cite the associated study and this archived software release."
title: "Data and code for: Placement can reverse the fragmentation-time response to localized mobility suppression in a welded nanowire junction"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Alzanki"
    given-names: "Ayas"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3121-3778"
    affiliation: "Energy and Building Research Center, Kuwait Institute for Scientific Research"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: 2026-08-21
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/AJayQ8/selective-mobility-placement-nanowire-fragmentation"
url: "https://github.com/AJayQ8/selective-mobility-placement-nanowire-fragmentation"
abstract: >-
  Code, normalized data, provenance, figures, and zero-step validation analyses
  for a conserved diffuse-interface study showing that outward placement of
  otherwise identical low-mobility collars can reverse their fragmentation-time
  response. This release adds the audited pre-fragmentation morphology evidence,
  the CMS validation matrix, and preserved negative benchmark gates.
keywords:
  - phase field
  - conserved diffuse-interface transport
  - nanowire junction
  - localized mobility
  - fragmentation
  - first-passage time
  - kinetic patterning
